From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:25:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Write boards and posts

Pages that write: make a board and write a post, two forms.

- A form in board/forms.go embeds maago.Form and has a maago.Field[T]
  for each field. With model=Board it takes its rules (required,
  max=100, the label) from the model. They are not written twice
- GET draws the form and POST saves it, in two views. Both take the
  same In, whose maago:"form" field is the form: the empty form on GET
  still knows its fields' names and labels. Two lines in the routes,
  the same path:

      maago.GET("/boards/new", "board_new", NewBoard),
      maago.POST("/boards/new", "board_create", CreateBoard),

      func NewBoard(ctx context.Context, in NewBoardIn) (BoardFormPage, error)
      func CreateBoard(ctx context.Context, tx maago.Tx, in NewBoardIn) (maago.Result[BoardFormPage], error)

  When a GET and a POST split, the POST view is named after its route:
  board_create is CreateBoard. The two return the same page type, so
  they share its template
- A view that writes takes tx maago.Tx: it runs in the request's
  transaction. Pass tx to the generated functions as it is (InsertBoard,
  the queries): a maago.Tx is a maago.DB. What the view returns decides:
  maago.Show(page) draws the page (200) and commits, maago.SeeOther[P](url)
  commits and redirects (303), and an error rolls everything back (a
  404 too). The adapter draws the page before it commits, so a page that
  fails to draw rolls back too. maago gen refuses a maago.Tx on a GET
  route, and a view that takes both maago.Tx and maago.DB
- f.Valid() is true only on a POST that keeps every rule. Otherwise the
  view shows the same page again (200): each field's .Error has what is
  wrong, and its .Raw what was sent
- What only the database knows, such as a name already taken, the view
  asks with a query (board_name_taken.sql) and writes to f.Name.Error.
  The same goes for a post's title on its board (post_title_taken.sql).
  Without the question, the model's unique refuses the row as a 500
- Once saved, maago.SeeOther sends the browser to the new thing's page
  (303), so a reload does not send the form again
- A post's board comes from the path (/boards/{id}/posts/new), not the
  form: a board that is not there is a 404, on GET and POST

The transaction makes the view's writes all or none. It does not stop
two requests at once from asking first and both finding a title free:
the unique constraint then refuses the second.

When another site sends one of these forms, it gets a 403: maago.Handler
stops CSRF (it trusts only the origins in Config.Origins).

diff --git a/board/forms.go b/board/forms.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..6db3438
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/forms.go
@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+package board
+
+import "github.com/maago-web/maago"
+
+// BoardForm takes its fields' rules from the model: the name is required,
+// and at most 100 characters.
+type BoardForm struct {
+	maago.Form `maago:"model=Board"`
+	Name       maago.Field[string]
+}
+
+// PostForm is the post's title and body. The board comes from the path.
+type PostForm struct {
+	maago.Form `maago:"model=Post"`
+	Title      maago.Field[string]
+	Body       maago.Field[string]
+}
diff --git a/board/queries/board_name_taken.sql b/board/queries/board_name_taken.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e2f58cf
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/queries/board_name_taken.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,7 @@
+-- name: BoardNameTaken :one Count
+-- How many boards have the name: 0 or 1.
+-- param: name string
+-- column: n int64
+SELECT count(*) AS n
+FROM board_board
+WHERE name = :name
diff --git a/board/queries/post_title_taken.sql b/board/queries/post_title_taken.sql
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..d28b47e
--- /dev/null
+++ b/board/queries/post_title_taken.sql
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+-- name: PostTitleTaken :one Count
+-- How many posts of the board have the title: 0 or 1.
+-- param: board_id int64
+-- param: title    string
+-- column: n int64
+SELECT count(*) AS n
+FROM board_post
+WHERE board_id = :board_id AND title = :title
